From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marcho78 <marcho78@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] memory: tegra210-emc: Apply the requested refresh rate

tegra210_emc_set_refresh() compares the requested refresh with
emc->refresh but never stores it, and tegra210_emc_adjust_timing(),
which speeds the refresh up, switches on emc->refresh: as the DRAM's
MR4 reports it hotter, the poller asks for 2x and 4x refresh, and the
timing stays at nominal. Store it before the timing is adjusted.

Throttling also falls back to the nominal table, at nominal refresh,
when the board has no derated table. Use 4x refresh then, the most the
timing allows.
---
diff --git a/drivers/memory/tegra/tegra210-emc-core.c b/drivers/memory/tegra/tegra210-emc-core.c
index e8d4cd8fd..91beaf364 100644
--- a/drivers/memory/tegra/tegra210-emc-core.c
+++ b/drivers/memory/tegra/tegra210-emc-core.c
@@ -777,11 +777,21 @@ int tegra210_emc_set_refresh(struct tegra210_emc *emc,
 	if (refresh > TEGRA210_EMC_REFRESH_THROTTLE)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/*
+	 * Throttling moves to the derated table. Without one, refresh as often
+	 * as the timing allows instead: the DRAM is at its hottest.
+	 */
+	if (refresh == TEGRA210_EMC_REFRESH_THROTTLE && !emc->derated)
+		refresh = TEGRA210_EMC_REFRESH_4X;
+
 	if (refresh == emc->refresh)
 		return 0;
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&emc->lock, flags);
 
+	/* tegra210_emc_adjust_timing() reads it, here and at clock changes */
+	emc->refresh = refresh;
+
 	if (refresh == TEGRA210_EMC_REFRESH_THROTTLE && emc->derated)
 		timings = emc->derated;
 	else
